<div class="page-header"><h1 class="page-header__title">Supported Applications</h1><p class="page-header__subtitle">Check whether your project fits the current pilot.</p></div>
<div class="compatibility-grid">
  <section class="card"><div class="card__body"><h2>Supported</h2><ul><li>Static HTML, CSS, and JavaScript</li><li>Node.js and Express</li><li>React and Vue static builds</li><li>Legacy Next.js applications</li></ul></div></section>
  <section class="card"><div class="card__body"><h2>Not currently supported</h2><ul><li>Python, PHP, or Java</li><li>Docker Compose</li><li>Arbitrary container images</li><li>Privileged containers, GPUs, game servers, proxies, or mining workloads</li></ul></div></section>
</div>
<section class="card mt-6"><div class="card__body"><h2>Invitation-only pilot (paused)</h2><p>These runtimes are being tested with invited projects only. They are not open to new projects while the pilot is paused.</p><ul><li>npm-based Next.js standard, standalone, and static-export applications</li><li>Python apps built with Flask, FastAPI, or Django</li><li>PHP sites and Laravel apps</li><li>Java Spring Boot apps built with Maven or Gradle</li></ul><p>Next.js server modes are single-instance. ISR and cache data are container-local and are not preserved across replacement or rollback.</p></div></section>
<div class="card mt-6"><div class="card__body"><h2>Before you start</h2><p>Your project should be in GitHub, use npm with a committed <code class="code-inline">package-lock.json</code>, and expose a supported start or static-build workflow. Private server secrets are runtime-only and are not exposed to <code class="code-inline">next build</code>.</p><a href="/auth/create-account" class="button button--primary mt-4">Create Account</a></div></div>
